{
 "topic": "aging",
 "axis_notes": {
  "workemployment": "Ill-defined: pro and con are compatible (con only says employment alone is insufficient). Read as: pro = treats stable employment/wages/work-environment as a key fertility lever; con = doubts economic/employment causes of low fertility (only 3553).",
  "educationcost": "Core: support free/cheaper education (preschool to university) as child policy. Con = cautious/opposes free education; members who say waitlist (待機児童) must come before preschool 無償化 were labelled con (priority/quality objection, not cost), neutral if they also back other free education.",
  "budgetpriority": "Core: prioritise childcare/child budget over defence spending (pro) vs defence is essential first (con). Members worried about burden of both defence and childcare without choosing = na/neutral. No con found.",
  "parentalleave": "Core: expand/promote parental leave for both parents (pro) vs concern about burden on firms (con). Members critical only of design or skeptical of fertility effect but backing uptake still pro; no con found."
 },
